# Evidence-First Project Execution

- Before choosing work, load the compact handoff bootstrap. Read a long-term plan,
  milestone, report, or log only when the handoff points to its exact relevant
  section or a material conflict requires expansion.
- Treat user instructions, repository files, Git state, and reproducible command
  output as truth; conversation memory and model summaries are claims to verify.
- Within an approved active milestone, execute the single recorded next task. If
  no milestone is active, do not invent one.
- After each verified unit, record what completed, what remains or failed, its
  effect on later work, and one exact next task. Store detail in the active plan
  or report; keep status and handoff summaries bounded.
- Implementation without the contract's tests or evidence is not complete.
- Continue automatically only inside the recorded scope and authority boundary.
- Stop for material goal, architecture, acceptance, privacy, security, license,
  external-write, destructive-action, or unresolved source-of-truth conflicts.
- Use `.cursor/rules/model-handoff.mdc` whenever responsibility or model changes.
